From 4cc76a6a854f99487fd27c555e23397db733bd48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for asa582)" <ahmadsb101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:46:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] v2023 m_axi timing model (Vitis HLS 2023.2 adapter +
 cosim memory)

Adds LSIM_AXI_MODEL=v2023 (default stays v2021, bit-identical to upstream):
per-interface adapter config (set_axi_config), reads split into bursts at
max_read_burst_length/4 KB with a per-burst read credit, and a per-burst AW
node for writes (request gate, last write, serial bus drain, one-burst
throttle FIFO, write credit), kernel write stalls on WBUFF + throttle depth,
and write responses from the last burst's B. Delay constants are runtime
settable (set_axi_constants) for fitting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
